CommitDate: Fri Jul 31 23:52:35 2026 -0300

    [kyo-scheduler] shutdown: stop the InternalClock
    
    Scheduler.shutdown() stopped the cycle task, the blocking monitor, and both
    regulators but never stopped the InternalClock, so a shut-down scheduler left
    its clock update thread pinned on the clock executor, contradicting shutdown's
    "stops all internal threads" contract. A process that repeatedly constructs and
    shuts down schedulers leaks one clock thread each; when the clock executor is a
    shared bounded pool this eventually exhausts it, starving later schedulers'
    monitor and regulator tasks of a pool thread.
    
    Stop the clock in shutdown().

 kyo-scheduler/jvm-native/src/main/scala/kyo/scheduler/Scheduler.scala | 1 +
